  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One credential store",
      "items": [
        "the Keychain item is written once, right after the server exchanges the code — the token never touches UserDefaults, the logs or the bundle",
        "the Domain declares SessionStore and TokenProvider; the Data target implements them over the Keychain, so no Domain code calls SecItem APIs",
        "sign out wipes the Keychain and the GRDB user data together"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The sign-in path",
      "items": [
        "Sign in with Apple, passkeys, or OIDC + PKCE in ASWebAuthenticationSession — never an embedded webview login",
        "the device sends the authorization code and the PKCE verifier; the exchange happens server-side",
        "the App Attest assertion travels as a risk signal the server may weigh — it never blocks on the client"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Refresh and refusal",
      "items": [
        "a 401 triggers a refresh; the rotated token replaces the stored one, so a replayed refresh is refused server-side",
        "a 403 becomes the rendered .forbidden state — the client hides the action it cannot perform, and the server is the only authority",
        "ATS stays on and there is no arbitrary-loads exception without a documented reason"
      ]
    }
  ]
